  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows > 0 else 0\n    \n    best_interior = None\n    best_area = 0\n    \n    for r1 in range(rows):\n        for c1 in range(cols):\n            v = grid[r1][c1]\n            \n            # Extend right to find top-right corner\n            c2 = c1\n            while c2 + 1 < cols and grid[r1][c2 + 1] == v:\n                c2 += 1\n            \n            if c2 == c1:\n                continue\n            \n            # Extend down to find bottom-left corner\n            r2 = r1\n            while r2 + 1 < rows and grid[r2 + 1][c1] == v:\n                r2 += 1\n            \n            if r2 == r1:\n                continue\n            \n            # Check if bottom-right corner matches\n            if grid[r2][c2] != v:\n                continue\n            \n            # Verify bottom edge is solid\n            valid = True\n            for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                if grid[r2][c] != v:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if not valid:\n                continue\n            \n            # Verify right edge is solid\n            for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n                if grid[r][c2] != v:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if not valid:\n                continue\n            \n            # Extract interior\n            interior_height = r2 - r1 - 1\n            interior_width = c2 - c1 - 1\n            \n            if interior_height > 0 and interior_width > 0:\n                area = interior_height * interior_width\n                if area > best_area:\n                    best_area = area\n                    # Extract the interior subgrid\n                    best_interior = [row[c1+1:c2] for row in grid[r1+1:r2]]\n    \n    return best_interior if best_interior is not None else grid\n```",
